IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-vintage`

-- je54-v1-arts-6-16-17: Articles 6, 16 and 17 of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, which are in V1 (1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021) only.
-- The Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021) deleted all three from 28 September 2021; the placeholders "6 [8]", "16 [17]" and "17 [18]" of the later texts are inert and every function here refuses for them, naming
-- that Law.  Whatever replaces these Articles after that date is in the 2021 Law, which this row does not encode.  A question about a day before 1 January 2019 refuses (no text is deposited).
-- Selecting date: the day the repeal takes effect, the power is exercised or the enactment ceases (the day the fact occurred); the caller reads the text for that day.
-- Instants are DATETIME, as in je54-art01-commencement, so that "until the substituted provisions come into operation" can be answered at the moment of operation and not only by day.

§ `The text in which these Articles are`

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:25 | 6 Effect of repeal
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:70 | 16 Exercise of statutory powers before commencement of enactment
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:73 | 17 Effect of repeal and re-enactment, and expiry
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Articles 6, 16 and 17, as they read before 28 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:25), (src:l_17_1954_20210927:70), (src:l_17_1954_20210927:73)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Articles 6, 16 and 17 are in the text` v MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `V1, 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:25 | 6 Effect of repeal
-- src:25 | 6 [8]
