§ `Article 6: Effect of repeal`

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:26 | (1) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, repeals a repealing enactment, it shall not be construed as reviving any enactment previously repealed, unless words are added reviving that enactment.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 6(1) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:26)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 6(1): the enactment does not repeal a repealing enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 6(1) deals only where an enactment repeals a repealing enactment"

-- 6(1): where an enactment repeals a repealing enactment, it is not construed as reviving any enactment previously repealed, unless words are added reviving that enactment.  TRUE: the Article bars revival.
-- FALSE: words are added, so the bar does not apply and the added words decide.  Article 6(1) has no "unless the contrary intention appears"; the exception is the added words.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:26 | (1) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, repeals a repealing enactment, it shall not be construed as reviving any enactment previously repealed, unless words are added reviving that enactment.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 6(1) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:26)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the enactment repeals a repealing enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `words are added reviving the enactment previously repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 6(1): the repeal is not construed as reviving the enactment previously repealed` v `the enactment repeals a repealing enactment` `words are added reviving the enactment previously repealed` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `Articles 6, 16 and 17 are in the text` v THEN `Article 6: deleted from 28 September 2021`
           IF NOT `the enactment repeals a repealing enactment` THEN `Article 6(1): the enactment does not repeal a repealing enactment`
           OTHERWISE NOT `words are added reviving the enactment previously repealed`

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:27 | (2) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, repeals wholly or partially any former enactment and substitutes provisions for the enactment repealed, the repealed provisions shall remain in force until the substituted provisions come into operation.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 6(2) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:27)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 6(2): the enactment does not substitute provisions for the enactment repealed` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 6(2) deals only where an enactment repeals wholly or partially a former enactment and substitutes provisions for the enactment repealed"

-- 6(2): where an enactment repeals a former enactment, wholly or partially, and substitutes provisions for the enactment repealed, the repealed provisions remain in force until the substituted provisions come into operation.
-- The substituted provisions come into operation at an instant (the caller reads it from Article 1(4)), or not yet (NOTHING).  At the instant itself the substituted provisions are in operation, so the repealed provisions are not in force.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:27 | (2) Where an enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, repeals wholly or partially any former enactment and substitutes provisions for the enactment repealed, the repealed provisions shall remain in force until the substituted provisions come into operation.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 6(2) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:27)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the enactment substitutes provisions for those it repeals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instant asked about` IS A DATETIME
      `the instant at which the substituted provisions come into operation` IS A MAYBE DATETIME
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 6(2): the repealed provisions remain in force` v `the enactment substitutes provisions for those it repeals` `the instant asked about` `the instant at which the substituted provisions come into operation` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `Articles 6, 16 and 17 are in the text` v THEN `Article 6: deleted from 28 September 2021`
           IF NOT `the enactment substitutes provisions for those it repeals` THEN `Article 6(2): the enactment does not substitute provisions for the enactment repealed`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `the instant at which the substituted provisions come into operation`
               WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
               WHEN JUST operation THEN DATETIME_SERIAL `the instant asked about` LESS THAN DATETIME_SERIAL operation

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:28 | (3) Where an enactment which has been amended by any other enactment is repealed, such repeal shall, unless the contrary intention appears, include the repeal of all those provisions of other enactments by which the first-mentioned enactment was amended.[6]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 6(3) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:28)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 6(3): the enactment repealed was not amended by another enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 6(3) deals only where an enactment which has been amended by any other enactment is repealed"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:28 | (3) Where an enactment which has been amended by any other enactment is repealed, such repeal shall, unless the contrary intention appears, include the repeal of all those provisions of other enactments by which the first-mentioned enactment was amended.[6]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 6(3) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:28)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 6(3): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 6(3) does not say what the repeal then includes"

-- 6(3): where an enactment which has been amended by any other enactment is repealed, the repeal includes, unless the contrary intention appears, the repeal of all those provisions of other enactments by which
-- the first-mentioned enactment was amended.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:28 | (3) Where an enactment which has been amended by any other enactment is repealed, such repeal shall, unless the contrary intention appears, include the repeal of all those provisions of other enactments by which the first-mentioned enactment was amended.[6]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 6(3) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:28)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `an enactment that has been amended by another enactment is repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is one of those by which the repealed enactment was amended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 6(3): the repeal includes the repeal of the provision` v `an enactment that has been amended by another enactment is repealed` `the provision is one of those by which the repealed enactment was amended` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `Articles 6, 16 and 17 are in the text` v THEN `Article 6: deleted from 28 September 2021`
           IF NOT `an enactment that has been amended by another enactment is repealed` THEN `Article 6(3): the enactment repealed was not amended by another enactment`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 6(3): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE `the provision is one of those by which the repealed enactment was amended`

§ `Article 16: Exercise of statutory powers before commencement of enactment`

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:71 | (1) Where any Law passed after the commencement of this Law is not to come into operation immediately on the passing thereof, and confers power to make any appointment, to pass any enactment, to give notices, to prescribe forms or to do any other thing for the purposes of the Law, that power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised at any time after the passing of the Law, so far as may be necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Law into operation at the date of commencement, subject to the restriction that any enactment passed under the power shall not, unless the contrary intention appears in the Law, or the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation, come into operation until the Law comes into operation.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 16(1) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:71)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 16: the instrument is neither a Law nor Regulations passed by the States` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 16 deals with a Law passed after the commencement of the Law and, by Article 16(2), with Regulations passed by the States"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:71 | (1) Where any Law passed after the commencement of this Law is not to come into operation immediately on the passing thereof, and confers power to make any appointment, to pass any enactment, to give notices, to prescribe forms or to do any other thing for the purposes of the Law, that power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised at any time after the passing of the Law, so far as may be necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Law into operation at the date of commencement, subject to the restriction that any enactment passed under the power shall not, unless the contrary intention appears in the Law, or the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation, come into operation until the Law comes into operation.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 16(1) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:71)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 16(1): the Law comes into operation immediately on its passing, or confers no power` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 16(1) deals only where a Law is not to come into operation immediately on its passing and confers power to make an appointment, to pass an enactment, to give notices, to prescribe forms or to do any other thing for the purposes of the Law"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:71 | (1) Where any Law passed after the commencement of this Law is not to come into operation immediately on the passing thereof, and confers power to make any appointment, to pass any enactment, to give notices, to prescribe forms or to do any other thing for the purposes of the Law, that power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised at any time after the passing of the Law, so far as may be necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Law into operation at the date of commencement, subject to the restriction that any enactment passed under the power shall not, unless the contrary intention appears in the Law, or the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation, come into operation until the Law comes into operation.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 16(1) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:71)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 16(1): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 16(1) does not say when the power may then be exercised"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:71 | (1) Where any Law passed after the commencement of this Law is not to come into operation immediately on the passing thereof, and confers power to make any appointment, to pass any enactment, to give notices, to prescribe forms or to do any other thing for the purposes of the Law, that power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised at any time after the passing of the Law, so far as may be necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Law into operation at the date of commencement, subject to the restriction that any enactment passed under the power shall not, unless the contrary intention appears in the Law, or the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation, come into operation until the Law comes into operation.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 16(1) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:71)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 16(1): the Law gives no time of day for its own commencement` MEANS
    REFUSE "the day alone does not show whether the power was exercised after the passing of the Law, or whether the Law was passed after the commencement of the Law on 21 August 1954, for which the Law gives no time of day"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:71 | (1) Where any Law passed after the commencement of this Law is not to come into operation immediately on the passing thereof, and confers power to make any appointment, to pass any enactment, to give notices, to prescribe forms or to do any other thing for the purposes of the Law, that power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised at any time after the passing of the Law, so far as may be necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Law into operation at the date of commencement, subject to the restriction that any enactment passed under the power shall not, unless the contrary intention appears in the Law, or the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation, come into operation until the Law comes into operation.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 16(1) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:71)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 16(1): the Law was passed before the commencement of the Law` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 16(1) deals only with a Law passed after the commencement of the Law on 21 August 1954; it does not say when a power conferred by a Law passed before that day may be exercised"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:71 | (1) Where any Law passed after the commencement of this Law is not to come into operation immediately on the passing thereof, and confers power to make any appointment, to pass any enactment, to give notices, to prescribe forms or to do any other thing for the purposes of the Law, that power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised at any time after the passing of the Law, so far as may be necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Law into operation at the date of commencement, subject to the restriction that any enactment passed under the power shall not, unless the contrary intention appears in the Law, or the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation, come into operation until the Law comes into operation.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 16(1) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:71)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 16(1): the power is exercised before the passing of the Law` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 16(1) says the power may be exercised at any time after the passing of the Law; it does not say whether the power may be exercised before the passing"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:71 | (1) Where any Law passed after the commencement of this Law is not to come into operation immediately on the passing thereof, and confers power to make any appointment, to pass any enactment, to give notices, to prescribe forms or to do any other thing for the purposes of the Law, that power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised at any time after the passing of the Law, so far as may be necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Law into operation at the date of commencement, subject to the restriction that any enactment passed under the power shall not, unless the contrary intention appears in the Law, or the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation, come into operation until the Law comes into operation.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 16(1) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:71)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 16(1): the exercise is not necessary or expedient for bringing the Law into operation` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 16(1) says the power may be exercised so far as may be necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Law into operation at the date of commencement; it does not say whether the power may be exercised for any other purpose"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:71 | (1) Where any Law passed after the commencement of this Law is not to come into operation immediately on the passing thereof, and confers power to make any appointment, to pass any enactment, to give notices, to prescribe forms or to do any other thing for the purposes of the Law, that power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised at any time after the passing of the Law, so far as may be necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Law into operation at the date of commencement, subject to the restriction that any enactment passed under the power shall not, unless the contrary intention appears in the Law, or the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation, come into operation until the Law comes into operation.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 16(1) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:71)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 16(1): the restriction does not apply, and the Article does not say when the enactment may then come into operation` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears in the Law, or the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation: Article 16(1) lifts its restriction and does not say when the enactment passed under the power may then come into operation"

-- 16(1): where a Law passed after the commencement of the Law is not to come into operation immediately on its passing, and confers power to do a thing for the purposes of the Law, that power may, unless the contrary
-- intention appears, be exercised at any time after the passing of the Law, so far as may be necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Law into operation at the date of commencement.
-- 16(2): Regulations passed by the States are treated in like manner.  "After the passing" and "after the commencement" are compared by day; on the same day the Article cannot say, and the function refuses.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:71 | (1) Where any Law passed after the commencement of this Law is not to come into operation immediately on the passing thereof, and confers power to make any appointment, to pass any enactment, to give notices, to prescribe forms or to do any other thing for the purposes of the Law, that power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised at any time after the passing of the Law, so far as may be necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Law into operation at the date of commencement, subject to the restriction that any enactment passed under the power shall not, unless the contrary intention appears in the Law, or the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation, come into operation until the Law comes into operation.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:72 | (2) This Article shall apply in relation to Regulations passed by the States in like manner as it applies in relation to a Law.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 16(1) and 16(2) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:71-72)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      instrument IS AN `Instrument dealt with by Article 16`
      `the day on which it was passed` IS A DATE
      `it is not to come into operation immediately on its passing and it confers a power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the power is exercised` IS A DATE
      `the exercise is necessary or expedient for bringing it into operation at the date of commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 16(1) and 16(2): the power may be exercised before the Law comes into operation` v instrument `the day on which it was passed` `it is not to come into operation immediately on its passing and it confers a power` `the day on which the power is exercised` `the exercise is necessary or expedient for bringing it into operation at the date of commencement` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `Articles 6, 16 and 17 are in the text` v THEN `Article 16: deleted from 28 September 2021`
           IF instrument EQUALS `some other instrument` THEN `Article 16: the instrument is neither a Law nor Regulations passed by the States`
           IF NOT `it is not to come into operation immediately on its passing and it confers a power` THEN `Article 16(1): the Law comes into operation immediately on its passing, or confers no power`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 16(1): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           IF `the day on which it was passed` EQUALS `the day on which the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 came into force` THEN `Article 16(1): the Law gives no time of day for its own commencement`
           IF `the day on which it was passed` LESS THAN `the day on which the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 came into force` THEN `Article 16(1): the Law was passed before the commencement of the Law`
           IF `the day on which the power is exercised` EQUALS `the day on which it was passed` THEN `Article 16(1): the Law gives no time of day for its own commencement`
           IF `the day on which the power is exercised` LESS THAN `the day on which it was passed` THEN `Article 16(1): the power is exercised before the passing of the Law`
           IF NOT `the exercise is necessary or expedient for bringing it into operation at the date of commencement` THEN `Article 16(1): the exercise is not necessary or expedient for bringing the Law into operation`
           OTHERWISE TRUE

-- 16(1), the restriction: any enactment passed under the power shall not, unless the contrary intention appears in the Law, or the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation, come into operation until the
-- Law comes into operation.  TRUE: the enactment may come into operation at the instant given.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:71 | (1) Where any Law passed after the commencement of this Law is not to come into operation immediately on the passing thereof, and confers power to make any appointment, to pass any enactment, to give notices, to prescribe forms or to do any other thing for the purposes of the Law, that power may, unless the contrary intention appears, be exercised at any time after the passing of the Law, so far as may be necessary or expedient for the purpose of bringing the Law into operation at the date of commencement, subject to the restriction that any enactment passed under the power shall not, unless the contrary intention appears in the Law, or the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation, come into operation until the Law comes into operation.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:72 | (2) This Article shall apply in relation to Regulations passed by the States in like manner as it applies in relation to a Law.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 16(1) and 16(2) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:71-72)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      instrument IS AN `Instrument dealt with by Article 16`
      `the instant at which the enactment passed under the power is to come into operation` IS A DATETIME
      `the instant at which the Law comes into operation` IS A DATETIME
      `a contrary intention appears in the Law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 16(1): the enactment passed under the power may come into operation at that instant` v instrument `the instant at which the enactment passed under the power is to come into operation` `the instant at which the Law comes into operation` `a contrary intention appears in the Law` `the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `Articles 6, 16 and 17 are in the text` v THEN `Article 16: deleted from 28 September 2021`
           IF instrument EQUALS `some other instrument` THEN `Article 16: the instrument is neither a Law nor Regulations passed by the States`
           IF `a contrary intention appears in the Law` OR `the contrary is necessary for bringing the Law into operation` THEN `Article 16(1): the restriction does not apply, and the Article does not say when the enactment may then come into operation`
           OTHERWISE NOT (DATETIME_SERIAL `the instant at which the enactment passed under the power is to come into operation` LESS THAN DATETIME_SERIAL `the instant at which the Law comes into operation`)

§ `Article 17: Effect of repeal and re-enactment, and expiry`

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:74 | (1) Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, repeals and re-enacts, with or without modification, any provisions of a former enactment, references in any other enactment to the provisions so repealed shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as references to the provisions so re-enacted.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 17(1) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:74)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 17(1): the enactment does not repeal and re-enact provisions of a former enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 17(1) deals only where an enactment repeals and re-enacts, with or without modification, provisions of a former enactment"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:74 | (1) Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, repeals and re-enacts, with or without modification, any provisions of a former enactment, references in any other enactment to the provisions so repealed shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as references to the provisions so re-enacted.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 17(1) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:74)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 17(1): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 17(1) does not say what a reference to the provisions repealed is then taken to be"

-- 17(1): references in any other enactment to the provisions repealed are, unless the contrary intention appears, construed as references to the provisions re-enacted, with or without modification.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:74 | (1) Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, repeals and re-enacts, with or without modification, any provisions of a former enactment, references in any other enactment to the provisions so repealed shall, unless the contrary intention appears, be construed as references to the provisions so re-enacted.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 17(1) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:74)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the enactment repeals and re-enacts provisions of a former enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 17(1): a reference in another enactment to the provisions repealed is construed as a reference to the provisions re-enacted` v `the enactment repeals and re-enacts provisions of a former enactment` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `Articles 6, 16 and 17 are in the text` v THEN `Article 17: deleted from 28 September 2021`
           IF NOT `the enactment repeals and re-enacts provisions of a former enactment` THEN `Article 17(1): the enactment does not repeal and re-enact provisions of a former enactment`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 17(1): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:75 | (2) Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, repeals any other enactment, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the repeal shall not –
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 17(2) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:75)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 17(2): the enactment does not repeal any other enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 17(2) deals only where an enactment repeals any other enactment"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:82 | (3) The provisions of paragraph (2) shall apply in relation to an enactment which has expired in like manner as they apply in relation to an enactment which has been repealed.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 17(3) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:82)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 17(3): the Article does not say whether paragraph (2) applies to an enactment that ceased in some other way` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 17(3) says paragraph (2) applies to an enactment that has expired as it applies to one that has been repealed; it does not say whether it applies to an enactment that ceased in any other way"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:75 | (2) Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, repeals any other enactment, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the repeal shall not –
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 17(2) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:75)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 17(2): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 17(2) does not say what the repeal then does"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:75 | (2) Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, repeals any other enactment, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the repeal shall not –
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:81 | and any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture or punishment may be imposed as if the repealing enactment had not been passed.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 17(2), closing words (src:l_17_1954_20210927:75), (src:l_17_1954_20210927:81)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 17(2): the Article does not say whether anything else may be done as if the repealing enactment had not been passed` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 17(2) says an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, and a penalty, forfeiture or punishment imposed, as if the repealing enactment had not been passed; it does not say whether anything else may be done as if it had not been passed"

-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:75 | (2) Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, repeals any other enactment, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the repeal shall not –
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:76 | (a) revive anything not in force or not existing at the time at which the repeal takes effect;
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:77 | (b) affect the previous operation of any enactment so repealed or anything duly done or suffered under any enactment so repealed;
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:78 | (c) affect any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under any enactment so repealed;
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:79 | (d) affect any penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of any offence committed against any enactment so repealed; or
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:80 | (e) affect any investigation, legal proceedings or remedy in respect of any such right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment as aforesaid,
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 17(2) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:75-80)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 17(2): the Article does not say whether the repeal has some other effect` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 17(2) lists the things the repeal does not do; it does not say whether the repeal has any other effect"

-- 17(2): where an enactment repeals any other enactment, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the repeal does not (a) revive anything not in force or not existing when the repeal takes effect; (b) affect the
-- previous operation of the enactment repealed or anything duly done or suffered under it; (c) affect any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it; (d) affect any penalty,
-- forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence against it; or (e) affect any investigation, legal proceedings or remedy in respect of any such right, ....  TRUE: the repeal does not do the thing.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:75 | (2) Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, repeals any other enactment, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the repeal shall not –
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:76 | (a) revive anything not in force or not existing at the time at which the repeal takes effect;
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:77 | (b) affect the previous operation of any enactment so repealed or anything duly done or suffered under any enactment so repealed;
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:78 | (c) affect any right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under any enactment so repealed;
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:79 | (d) affect any penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of any offence committed against any enactment so repealed; or
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:80 | (e) affect any investigation, legal proceedings or remedy in respect of any such right, privilege, obligation, liability, penalty, forfeiture or punishment as aforesaid,
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 17(2) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:75-80)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the enactment repeals another enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      effect IS AN `Effect of a repeal`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 17(2): the repeal does not` v `the enactment repeals another enactment` effect `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `Articles 6, 16 and 17 are in the text` v THEN `Article 17: deleted from 28 September 2021`
           IF NOT `the enactment repeals another enactment` THEN `Article 17(2): the enactment does not repeal any other enactment`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 17(2): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER effect
               WHEN `some other effect` THEN `Article 17(2): the Article does not say whether the repeal has some other effect`
               OTHERWISE TRUE

-- 17(2), closing words: any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture or punishment may be imposed, as if the repealing enactment
-- had not been passed.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:75 | (2) Where any enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, repeals any other enactment, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the repeal shall not –
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:81 | and any such investigation, legal proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced, and any such penalty, forfeiture or punishment may be imposed as if the repealing enactment had not been passed.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 17(2), closing words (src:l_17_1954_20210927:75), (src:l_17_1954_20210927:81)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the enactment repeals another enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `Thing done as if the repealing enactment had not been passed`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 17(2): the thing may be done as if the repealing enactment had not been passed` v `the enactment repeals another enactment` thing `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `Articles 6, 16 and 17 are in the text` v THEN `Article 17: deleted from 28 September 2021`
           IF NOT `the enactment repeals another enactment` THEN `Article 17(2): the enactment does not repeal any other enactment`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 17(2): a contrary intention appears, and the Article does not decide`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER thing
               WHEN `something else` THEN `Article 17(2): the Article does not say whether anything else may be done as if the repealing enactment had not been passed`
               OTHERWISE TRUE

-- 17(3): the provisions of paragraph (2) apply to an enactment which has expired in like manner as to one which has been repealed.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:82 | (3) The provisions of paragraph (2) shall apply in relation to an enactment which has expired in like manner as they apply in relation to an enactment which has been repealed.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 17(3) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:82)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      how IS A `How an enactment ceased`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 17(3): paragraph (2) applies to the enactment` v how MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `Articles 6, 16 and 17 are in the text` v THEN `Article 17: deleted from 28 September 2021`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER how
               WHEN `the enactment ceased in some other way` THEN `Article 17(3): the Article does not say whether paragraph (2) applies to an enactment that ceased in some other way`
               OTHERWISE TRUE
